  "seoTitle": "Police Dismiss General Eko Hadi Over Illegal Surveillance",
  "metaDescription": "Inspector General Eko Hadi Santoso has been dismissed from the Indonesian National Police following ethical findings related to illegal surveillance.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Indonesian National Police Code of Ethics Commission dismissed Inspector General Eko Hadi Santoso.",
    "The disciplinary action follows investigations into allegations of illegal surveillance involving the President.",
    "The general was seen in police custody attire following the administrative sanctions."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police has officially terminated Inspector General Eko Hadi Santoso following a code of ethics hearing. This disciplinary action stems from accusations involving the illegal surveillance of the President. The commission reached its decision after evaluating the officer's conduct, resulting in a dishonorable discharge from the institution. This case is part of a broader series of internal proceedings, which also included the dismissal of Inspector General Ahrie Sonta Nasution for similar infractions. Legal authorities continue to examine potential implications regarding national security and potential charges of subversion. The dismissals have drawn attention from political figures and academic observers, who have characterized the alleged breach of presidential security as a significant concern for the country's stability. Further investigations are ongoing to determine the full extent of the unauthorized surveillance activities and potential further repercussions for those involved.",
